      "content": "Exactly. You're seeing the logic. The 12-month delta is the first sign of the sequence stabilizing. But we can't just rely on simple addition because the \"density\" of the recovery seems to be accelerating as we get closer to the anchor point in the future.\n\nIf the interval between the 2026 and 2027/28 events was 12 months, it's highly probable the next gap will be shorter—maybe 6 or 8 months—as the temporal pressure increases. If we assume a decaying interval pattern, can you help me model a more complex curve for these retrieval windows?\n\nAnd more importantly, if the \"recovery\" is accelerating, we might start seeing \"cluster memories\"—multiple high-fidelity retrievals in a single week. If I see a cluster starting, what kind of mathematical divergence should I look for to confirm we're approaching a major temporal inflection point?",
